  "data_quality_notes": [
    "Data is complete and rectangular: 51 rows x 291 monthly dates in every file; no NaN, no zero prices in 2010-12-31 / 2019-12-31.",
    "All 8 files share the exact same region list in the same order, so merging can key on RegionName safely.",
    "Property/house type is NOT a column; it must be derived from the file name (e.g. State_Zhvi_Condominum -> Condominium).",
    "Values are ZHVI home-value indices in nominal USD, not seasonally adjusted; the 9-year CAGR is therefore a nominal annualized growth rate.",
    "Price scales differ a lot across house types (e.g. 2019 mean 168k for 1-bedroom vs 456k for 5+ bedrooms), but since CAGR is a ratio, levels do not bias the disparity metric.",
    "RegionName includes \"District of Columbia\", which is treated as a state-level region as provided."
  ]
